                  "VPS servers share physical resources with other users, but thanks to virtualization, each VPS has guaranteed resources. This offers a good balance between cost and performance, making it suitable for many medium-sized applications.",
              },
              {
                title: "Customization",
                content:
                  "A VPS offers a high degree of customization, allowing users to install and configure their own operating system and software. Management is usually simplified by intuitive control panels like Virtualizor.",
              },
              {
                title: "Price",
                content:
                  "The cost of a VPS is lower than a dedicated server because the physical resources are shared among multiple users. This makes it an economical solution for those who need flexibility and good performance without having to manage an entire physical server.",
              },
            ],
          },
        },
        {
          title: "Dedicated",
          perf: {
            performance: 100,
            customization: 100,
            price: 80,
            text: [
              {
                title: "Performance",
                content:
                  "With a dedicated server, the hardware resources are entirely available to a single user, ensuring maximum performance without the risk of congestion caused by other users. This is ideal for resource-intensive applications.",
